<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>L'Hopital's Rule: Evaluating a Limit</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p></p><p>Use L'Hopital's Rule to evaluate \(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@aa@}} {@fx@}.\)</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><h3><b>Worked Solution</b></h3></p>
<p>The given function is: \(\displaystyle f(x) =  {@fx@}\).</p>
<p>And we are asked to find: \(\displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} f(x)\)</p>
<p><b>Step 1:</b> Substitute \(x={@aa@}\) into \(f(x)\):</p>
<p> Evaluating \( {@top@} \) at \( x={@aa@} \)  yields to  \(0\).</p>
<p> Evaluating \( {@bot@}  \) at \(x={@aa@} \) yields to \(0\).</p>
<p>We can observe that both the numerator and the denominator have resulted to \(\displaystyle f({@aa@}) = \frac{0}{0}\). This indicates that the limit is of the form \(\frac{0}{0}\).</p>
<p><b>Step 2:</b> Apply L'Hôpital's Rule:</p>
<p>To use L'Hôpital's Rule, we take the derivative of both the numerator and denominator with respect to \(x\) and then evaluate the limit again. That is,
<p>\( \begin{align}
 \displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} f(x) =  \displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} \frac{({@top@})'}{({@bot@})'}
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p>Let's find the derivatives;</p>
<p>The derivative of the numerator \({@top@}\) is: </p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
({@top@})' & = \displaystyle \frac{d}{dx} \left[{@top@}\right] \\
& ={@dtop@} 
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p>The derivative of the denominator \({@bot@}\) is:</p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
({@bot@})' & = \displaystyle \frac{d}{dx} \left[{@bot@}\right] \\
& ={@dbot@} 
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p><b>Step 3:</b> Evaluate the derivatives at \(x={@aa@}\):</p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
 \displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} f(x) & =  \displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} \frac{@dtop@}{@dbot@}\\
& = \frac{@valtop@}{@valbot@}
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p>Therefore, \(  \displaystyle \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} f(x) = {@ta@} \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
